{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Barry wrote 6 different numbers, one on each side of 3 cards, and laid the cards on a table, as shown. The sums of the two numbers on each of the three cards are equal. The three numbers on the hidden sides are prime numbers. What is the average of the hidden prime numbers? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d5a887c5efe5e48596399d86a16a3f95fe9b35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path card=((0,0)--(0,3)--(2,3)--(2,0)--cycle); draw(card, linewidth(1)); draw(shift(2.5,0)*card, linewidth(1)); draw(shift(5,0)*card, linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$44$&quot;, (1,1.5)); label(&quot;$59$&quot;, shift(2.5,0)*(1,1.5)); label(&quot;$38$&quot;, shift(5,0)*(1,1.5));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"108\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93357694305df9314ccb524a7952795d59901ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 15\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the sum of the two numbers on any card.  Then the hidden prime numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696cd1acfa893365d5c314ada5c94f123c3a44da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77655ed5c64bda9233912de4ffa73021ab78844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b600d19584fcc31cde07a29abcbc5fb38f88927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> were even, then both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696cd1acfa893365d5c314ada5c94f123c3a44da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b600d19584fcc31cde07a29abcbc5fb38f88927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> would be even, which is impossible since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only even prime number.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77655ed5c64bda9233912de4ffa73021ab78844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is even and prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627f60a47cd8a31574e8b7256fdc83132686a889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-59=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daff83a519eed2764682d500bff71196a0132dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Thus the hidden prime numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so their average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4e3eae14227dc4e7aae77699a067ce3a447824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17+2+23}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number on the other side of the card showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.  Then the sum of the two numbers on each card is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e247b2d2e1695dcb30c2e5ee02e06919ceee7e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, so the number on the other side of the card showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe61e5b80572ad5a200a0d9cd354ce12a8c7800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265d332a4c4b51198e0afd69cac1c5e7041bdc02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> while the number on the other side of the card showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41be156ba98071197428779c0cdc7ab3510fc51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 6$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the average of the hidden numbers.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61de7a90c34a28ae2af364edf58f3957dba0a706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a =\\frac{1}{3}\\left(x+(x-21)+(x-6)\\right)=x-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"307\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a49aa69e80a7d3fa665fbe5e422e8cec740ab66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed8d6523d734dd0215a21a42d22bcc51066605d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is prime.\n</p><p>Of the answer choices, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af9f9bef8b96a0874ac4ae059fd8536f337ef467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" /> yields a prime value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed8d6523d734dd0215a21a42d22bcc51066605d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say that the 3 hidden prime numbers are x, y and z for cards 1, 2, and 3 respectively. \nTherefore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/78088c805894ec953bbd62b7885898d0c39553c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+44 = z+38 = y+59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"17\" />, y=x-15, z=x+6. Now we note that if y is odd, then x must be even and z must be even too, which won't work since 2 is the only distinct even prime. Therefore, y must be even so y must be 2 so x=17, z=23 and the average is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c165d76d48bb0213f357381693fa50f976b8707a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{42}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I8E7XUYlIFI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I8E7XUYlIFI</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Fa6TV3b_PzY\">https://youtu.be/Fa6TV3b_PzY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8\">2006 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016232437\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 237/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2239/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 136/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6188/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.067  